cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its documented workflow, please cite it as follows."
title: "SmartFallMM: Multimodal Fall Detection and Knowledge Distillation"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
authors:
  - family-names: Dhar
    given-names: Pratyay
abstract: >-
  Research software for examining SmartFallMM-based binary fall-detection
  experiments with inertial Transformer students, multimodal teacher models,
  and knowledge distillation. The repository preserves the original Kaggle
  notebook and its recorded metrics while providing a portable PyTorch pipeline,
  synthetic software checks, and an explicit scientific limitations audit.
keywords:
  - fall detection
  - SmartFallMM
  - multimodal learning
  - knowledge distillation
  - wearable sensors
  - human activity recognition
  - deep learning
  - PyTorch
